<item><title>Sierra Leone charcoal trade cuts trees as clean-cooking access stays low</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-charcoal-trade-cuts-trees-as-clean-cooking-a237a3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-charcoal-trade-cuts-trees-as-clean-cooking-a237a3/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>The government’s National Energy Compact says only 15% of the population has access to clean cooking, while charcoal supports some families’ livelihoods.</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:43:36 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" length="34790" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Sierra Leone debate questions whether vice president can succeed president</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-debate-questions-whether-vice-president-can-b42fab/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-debate-questions-whether-vice-president-can-b42fab/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>An analysis argues that past officeholders lacked a clear route to succession, citing Solomon Berewa’s 2007 defeat as the SLPP candidate.</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:43:36 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" length="34790" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Rokel community calls for inquiry into Container Junction crashes</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/rokel-community-calls-for-inquiry-into-container-junction-cc07bf/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/rokel-community-calls-for-inquiry-into-container-junction-cc07bf/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>Stakeholders say the junction on the Freetown-Waterloo Highway has recorded several fatal incidents over the years, and they want signs and no-parking zones installed.</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:40:19 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" length="34790" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
